# Component styles

One root class per component. Store it in script and reuse it in the template and SCSS. Do not repeat the class string in the template.

```ts
const rootClass = 'miraicms-admin-header'
```

```vue
<div :class="rootClass">
  <div :class="`${rootClass}__main`">
```

Elements are `` `${rootClass}__name` ``. Modifiers are `` `${rootClass}--name` ``. Combine several on one node: `:class="[rootClass, `${rootClass}--open`]"`.

Scoped SCSS uses the same name. Nest elements, modifiers, and states inside `#{$root}` (`&__main`, `&--open`, `&:hover`). Do not write flat selectors for the same component.

```scss
@use "../../assets/styles" as *;

$root: '.miraicms-admin-header';

#{$root} {
  display: flex;

  &__main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}
```

In the form and SEO packages, import tokens with `@use "miraicms-nuxt/styles" as *;`. Use `$color-*`, `$shadow-*`, and `math-rem()` from that import.

`@include miraicms-wrapper` wraps rules in `body#miraicms-body` so host CSS does not override the shell. Use it for admin pages and shell chrome: pages, menu, header, user menu, entry forms, notices. Put `#{$root}` inside the mixin. Leave fields, parts, and controls (buttons, selects) unwrapped. Follow the nearest component of the same kind.
